      "id": 28931,
      "name": "Spiff",
      "username": "Spiff",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-04-23T02:45:48.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>My interpretation = (a) the fowl card is played, which means that the top card of the villain deck is played too, since the two parts of the sentence are linked.  After that, (b) Hairtrigger Reflexes can destroy it.  The only way Hairtrigger Reflexes could interject itself into the middle of that fowl’s ability would be if both parts of the fowl ability were separated into individual sentences.</p>",
