      "id": 28939,
      "name": "pwatson1974",
      "username": "pwatson1974",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pwatson1974/{size}/1925_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-04-24T09:22:51.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;ketigid&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"ketigid\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think what you guys have said is the intended interaction between HtR and Fowls.</p>\n<p>However, for me, the strange wording is making me confused. Essentially, the question is, how do I interpret the trigger conditions? Between the phrases “Whenever a non-hero target enters play” and “When this card is played from the villain deck”, which triggers earlier with respect to the other? Or do both trigger at the same instant?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Well, technically, you would play a card from the villain deck before the card enters play, otherwise where did the non-hero target come from? So, I’d say the wording supports the inrepretation.</p>",
